ropriate simplification we get an  expression for the query complexity  so here is the theorem again  whose proof idea we outlined in  particular we  say that local list decoding  of codes from half minus epsilon  fraction of errors  need omega 1 over root epsilon queries  when epsilon is small even  if the code has very low rate and  even if we allow very large list sizes  our work leaves several open problems  one immediate open problem is to improve  the lower bound for the small epsilon  case from one over root epsilon  to maybe something better  our lower bound for the large epsilon  case can be extended  to handle decoding from erasures  uh specifically decoding from one minus  epsilon fraction of erasures  requires a bound of omega 1 over epsilon  we do not immediately see it is not  clear whether  the same can be done for the small  epsilon case  so what can we say about the small  epsilon case for  decoding from a ratios  a third very interesting question  would be whether non-black box  techniques can help  obtain better hardcore predicates from  heart functions  i would like to bring your attention to  the fact that  our work rolls out only  black box techniques and not non-black  box techniques  so this is a very interesting open  direction  in any case that is all i have got to  say  thank you for your time thank you

